WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.351
SMP Intelligence makes catalog lookups conversational.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.185
Here's the real Windows prototype.

00:00:07.185 --> 00:00:11.194
I ask which parts cross to an original equipment number.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:18.177
The matching parts appear in a conversation and a results table.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.057
Then I ask which vehicles they fit.

00:00:23.057 --> 00:00:26.345
Part numbers, usernames, and vehicle counts are blurred.

00:00:28.313 --> 00:00:32.308
The SQL tab shows the query proposed by the model.

00:00:32.308 --> 00:00:34.705
The backend checks it before execution.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.523
OpenAI proposes SQL.

00:00:38.523 --> 00:00:44.792
The database returns records, which stay local rather than going back to the model.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.721
Here's the public validator, adapted from the prototype.

00:00:48.721 --> 00:00:53.591
It parses the SQL and requires one SELECT statement per result.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:59.652
The checks limit which tables, functions, and SQL operations are allowed.

00:00:59.652 --> 00:01:01.642
Unsupported queries are rejected.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:05.504
The order matters.

00:01:05.504 --> 00:01:10.359
This pipeline validates the entire plan before making any database calls.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:19.877
So if the second query fails validation, the first query doesn't run either.

00:01:19.877 --> 00:01:21.192
No partial execution.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.460
This test checks exactly that.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:32.758
It supplies an invalid second query, then verifies that the database executor was called zero times.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.203
All 105 tests passed.

00:01:35.203 --> 00:01:40.766
They verify specific behaviors, not the accuracy of every AI answer.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:45.347
The original uses OpenAI, SQL Server, and WPF.

00:01:45.347 --> 00:01:52.118
The public sample uses an offline planner and fictional data, without company access.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:57.332
Explore the code, run the tests, or try the browser demo.

00:01:57.332 --> 00:01:59.219
This is a working prototype.
